From 35f88184a85e6c76bcac2b80da13a56b95e4d3c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Bozik <robertbozik@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 15:45:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Add lens shading correction to the
 GPU debayer

Under-display cameras and other small modules show strong shading that
differs between the colour channels: on the OV32C4 behind the OLED panel
of the Lenovo Yoga Slim 9 the corners lose 30 % of the brightness and
turn green, because red and blue fall off faster than green.

Add an Lsc algorithm to the software ISP IPA that reads a grid of
per-channel gains from the tuning file (measured on a flat field) and
passes it to the debayer through the parameters, and apply it in the
EGL debayer as a linearly filtered RGB8 texture right after the black
level subtraction. The CPU debayer warns once and ignores the table.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5 [Claude Code]
